{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00767",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.78,
      "end_seconds": 12.51,
      "duration_seconds": 10.73,
      "text": "Hi Jess, I'm Dana, the nurse. I did your urine dip when you came in, and I'll pass that to the doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.06,
      "end_seconds": 22.76,
      "duration_seconds": 7.7,
      "text": "Lovely. It's my fourth in six months, so I probably know what it'll say. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 25.93,
      "end_seconds": 33.75,
      "duration_seconds": 7.82,
      "text": "Hello Jess. It's the urine infections again. Tell me what's different this time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 37.2,
      "end_seconds": 46.97,
      "duration_seconds": 9.77,
      "text": "The usual, burning when I pee, going all the time, and a dull ache low down. It started on Monday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 50.2,
      "end_seconds": 55.24,
      "duration_seconds": 5.04,
      "text": "The dip showed leucocytes and nitrites, doctor, both positive."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.64,
      "end_seconds": 64.2,
      "duration_seconds": 6.56,
      "text": "Thanks, Dana. Jess, any fever, back pain, or blood in the urine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.42,
      "end_seconds": 72.7,
      "duration_seconds": 6.28,
      "text": "No fever. No back pain. A tiny bit of blood, I think, yesterday."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 75.35,
      "end_seconds": 79.09,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "Any discharge or new partner? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.73,
      "end_seconds": 85.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "No, nothing like that. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 88.3,
      "end_seconds": 93.88,
      "duration_seconds": 5.58,
      "text": "What do you drink, how much fluid in a day?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.32,
      "end_seconds": 102.19,
      "duration_seconds": 5.87,
      "text": "About a litre, I think. Mostly coffee, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.21,
      "end_seconds": 114.52,
      "duration_seconds": 9.31,
      "text": "That's not a lot. And do you hold on when you need to go? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 116.81,
      "end_seconds": 125.41,
      "duration_seconds": 8.6,
      "text": "At work, yes. I'm a teacher, and it's hard to get away. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.72,
      "end_seconds": 132.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "Let me press on your tummy. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.86,
      "end_seconds": 151.11,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 154.11,
      "end_seconds": 161.42,
      "duration_seconds": 7.31,
      "text": "A little tender over the bladder, and no tenderness over the kidneys."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 163.52,
      "end_seconds": 166.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "What does that mean? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.2,
      "end_seconds": 187.2,
      "duration_seconds": 17.0,
      "text": "It fits with a bladder infection again. But with four in six months, I can't rule out something that makes you prone to them, like a stone, or a problem with emptying the bladder."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 189.61,
      "end_seconds": 191.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Oh. Right. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 195.34,
      "end_seconds": 206.13,
      "duration_seconds": 10.79,
      "text": "I'd like to send a urine sample off to the lab, to grow the germ and see which antibiotic works."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 208.15,
      "end_seconds": 212.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "I can send that off now, doctor. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.06,
      "end_seconds": 223.54,
      "duration_seconds": 8.48,
      "text": "And I'd like to arrange a kidney and bladder ultrasound, to look for a cause."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.08,
      "end_seconds": 230.98,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Will that tell you something? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 233.7,
      "end_seconds": 241.88,
      "duration_seconds": 8.18,
      "text": "It will show whether the bladder empties fully, and whether there are stones. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 244.28,
      "end_seconds": 246.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "Right. And treatment? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.91,
      "end_seconds": 262.58,
      "duration_seconds": 13.67,
      "text": "I'll write that up when the lab has answered, because I want to choose the right drug, so drink plenty of water now, and a glass every hour."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 264.77,
      "end_seconds": 267.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "I can try. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.33,
      "end_seconds": 281.05,
      "duration_seconds": 11.72,
      "text": "Empty your bladder fully, wipe front to back, and go as soon as you need to, even at work."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 283.94,
      "end_seconds": 287.54,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "I'll tell my head. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 290.76,
      "end_seconds": 300.39,
      "duration_seconds": 9.63,
      "text": "If you get a fever, shaking, or back pain, come in the same day, because that could mean the kidneys."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.28,
      "end_seconds": 306.05,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "I will. Thanks, both. ~"
    }
  ]
}
